   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "תַּנְיָא, אָמַר רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא: כְּשֶׁהָיִיתִי עַם הָאָרֶץ אָמַרְתִּי: מִי יִתֵּן לִי תַּלְמִיד חָכָם וַאֲנַשְּׁכֶנּוּ כַּחֲמוֹר. אָמְרוּ לוֹ תַּלְמִידָיו: רַבִּי, אֱמוֹר כְּכֶלֶב! אָמַר לָהֶן: זֶה נוֹשֵׁךְ וְשׁוֹבֵר עֶצֶם, וְזֶה נוֹשֵׁךְ וְאֵינוֹ שׁוֹבֵר עֶצֶם.",
   "en": "«It was taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Akiva said: When I was an ignoramus I said: Who will give me a Torah scholar» so that «I will bite him like a donkey? His students said to him: Master, say» that you would bite him «like a dog! He said to them:» I specifically used that wording, as «this one,» a donkey, «bites and breaks bones, and that one,» a dog, «bites but does not break bones.»"
  }
 ],
